      <div class="callout key">
        <p>
          <span data-lang="pt"
            ><strong>A sacada:</strong> “terminais se ouvindo” =
            <em>mensagens numeradas num barramento</em>. O gerente
            <strong>despacha</strong> (cria um agente-filho com uma tarefa), o
            trabalhador <strong>devolve</strong> o resultado, e — o mais
            poderoso — pode <strong>perguntar</strong> ao gerente no meio do
            trabalho e <em>esperar</em> a resposta. Tudo num único processo
            Pi.</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            ><strong>The key idea:</strong> “terminals hearing each other” =
            <em>numbered messages on a bus</em>. The manager
            <strong>dispatches</strong> (creates a child agent with a task), the
            worker <strong>returns</strong> the result, and — most powerfully —
            can <strong>ask</strong> the manager mid-work and <em>wait</em> for
            the answer. All in a single Pi process.</span
          >
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="cite">
        <span data-lang="pt">Fonte:</span><span data-lang="en">Source:</span>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/nicobailon/pi-subagents"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          >pi-subagents</a
        >
        —
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >a extensão que adiciona subagentes, cadeias, paralelismo, async e
          coordenação por intercom ao Pi.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >the extension that adds subagents, chains, parallelism, async and
          intercom coordination to Pi.</span
        >
      </p>

      <!-- ============ 2. FOUR PATTERNS ============ -->
      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">2</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Quatro modos de coordenar</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Four ways to coordinate</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="kicker">
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >Toda orquestração é uma combinação destes quatro. Cada um responde a
          uma pergunta diferente sobre <em>quando</em> cada trabalhador
          age.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >Every orchestration is a mix of these four. Each answers a different
          question about <em>when</em> each worker acts.</span
        >
      </p>

      <div class="patterns">
        <div class="pattern" style="--accent: #8b6ff7">
          <h4>
            <span data-lang="pt">① Cadeia (sequência)</span
            ><span data-lang="en">① Chain (sequence)</span>
          </h4>
          <div class="when">
            <span data-lang="pt">Cada passo precisa do anterior.</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Each step needs the previous one.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="mini-tl">
            <span
              ><span data-lang="pt">gerente → A</span
              ><span data-lang="en">manager → A</span></span
            >
            <span
              ><span data-lang="pt">A devolve → B</span
              ><span data-lang="en">A returns → B</span></span
            >
            <span
              ><span data-lang="pt">B devolve → C</span
              ><span data-lang="en">B returns → C</span></span
            >
            <span
              ><span data-lang="pt">C devolve → gerente</span
              ><span data-lang="en">C returns → manager</span></span
            >
          </div>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt"
              >Turnos rígidos. A saída de um vira a entrada do próximo.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >Rigid turns. One’s output becomes the next one’s input.</span
            >
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="pattern" style="--accent: #2dd4bf">
          <h4>
            <span data-lang="pt">② Paralelo (leque)</span
            ><span data-lang="en">② Parallel (fan-out)</span>
          </h4>
          <div class="when">
            <span data-lang="pt">Passos independentes, ao mesmo tempo.</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Independent steps, at the same time.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="mini-tl">
            <span
              ><span data-lang="pt">gerente → A, B, C</span
              ><span data-lang="en">manager → A, B, C</span></span
            >
            <span
              ><span data-lang="pt">todos juntos</span
              ><span data-lang="en">all together</span></span
            >
            <span
              ><span data-lang="pt">A, B, C → gerente</span
              ><span data-lang="en">A, B, C → manager</span></span
            >
          </div>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt"
              >O gerente funde os resultados quando todos terminam.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >The manager merges the results when all finish.</span
            >
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="pattern" style="--accent: #60a5fa">
          <h4>
            <span data-lang="pt">③ Assíncrono (segundo plano)</span
            ><span data-lang="en">③ Async (background)</span>
          </h4>
          <div class="when">
            <span data-lang="pt">Dispare e continue; seja avisado ao fim.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >Fire and continue; get notified at the end.</span
            >
          </div>
          <div class="mini-tl">
            <span
              ><span data-lang="pt">despacha (bg)</span
              ><span data-lang="en">dispatch (bg)</span></span
            >
            <span
              ><span data-lang="pt">gerente faz outra coisa</span
              ><span data-lang="en">manager does other work</span></span
            >
            <span
              ><span data-lang="pt">🔔 notificação</span
              ><span data-lang="en">🔔 notification</span></span
            >
          </div>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt"
              >O gerente não bloqueia. Útil para trabalho longo.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >The manager doesn’t block. Good for long work.</span
            >
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="pattern" style="--accent: #fbbf24">
          <h4>
            <span data-lang="pt">④ Conversa (intercom)</span
            ><span data-lang="en">④ Conversation (intercom)</span>
          </h4>
          <div class="when">
            <span data-lang="pt">O trabalhador precisa de uma decisão.</span
            ><span data-lang="en">The worker needs a decision.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="mini-tl">
            <span
              ><span data-lang="pt">trabalhador trava</span
              ><span data-lang="en">worker halts</span></span
            >
            <span
              ><span data-lang="pt">gerente responde</span
              ><span data-lang="en">manager replies</span></span
            >
            <span
              ><span data-lang="pt">trabalhador retoma</span
              ><span data-lang="en">worker resumes</span></span
            >
          </div>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt"
              >É assim que um filho “ouve” o pai — e vice-versa.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >This is how a child “hears” its parent — and vice-versa.</span
            >
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="callout tip">
        <p>
          <span data-lang="pt"
            ><strong>Do eixos para decorar:</strong>
            <em>sequencial × paralelo</em> (quantos ao mesmo tempo) e
            <em>síncrono × assíncrono</em> (o gerente espera ou continua). O
            <em>intercom</em> é ortogonal — funciona em qualquer um dos
            quatro.</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            ><strong>Two axes to remember:</strong>
            <em>sequential × parallel</em> (how many at once) and
            <em>synchronous × asynchronous</em> (manager waits or continues).
            The <em>intercom</em> is orthogonal — it works in any of the
            four.</span
          >
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- ============ 3. INTERCOM ============ -->
      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">3</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Como eles “se ouvem” de verdade</span
        ><span data-lang="en">How they actually “hear” each other</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="kicker">
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >O barramento não é telepatia. São duas ferramentas que se cascam: o
          filho <strong>pergunta</strong>, o pai
          <strong>responde</strong>.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >The bus isn’t telepathy. It’s two tools that pair up: the child
          <strong>asks</strong>, the parent <strong>replies</strong>.</span
        >
      </p>

      <div class="grid cols-2">
        <div class="card" style="border-top: 4px solid var(--amber)">
          <h4>
            <span data-lang="pt">Filho → pai ·</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Child → parent ·</span>
            <code class="inline">contact_supervisor</code>
          </h4>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt"
              >O trabalhador trava e envia uma mensagem com um <em>motivo</em>.
              As razões <code>need_decision</code> e
              <code>interview_request</code> <strong>bloqueiam</strong>: o filho
              espera a resposta. <code>progress_update</code> é só um
              aviso.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >The worker halts and sends a message with a <em>reason</em>. The
              reasons <code>need_decision</code> and
              <code>interview_request</code> <strong>block</strong>: the child
              waits for the reply. <code>progress_update</code> is just a
              notice.</span
            >
          </p>
          <div class="sig">contact_supervisor({ reason, message })</div>
        </div>
        <div class="card" style="border-top: 4px solid var(--violet)">
          <h4>
            <span data-lang="pt">Pai → filho ·</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Parent → child ·</span>
            <code class="inline">subagent_supervisor</code>
          </h4>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt"
              >O gerente vê as perguntas pendentes com
              <code>action: "pending"</code> e responde com
              <code>action: "reply"</code>. Também pode
              <strong>guiar</strong> um filho vivo com <code>steer</code>.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >The manager sees pending questions with
              <code>action: "pending"</code> and replies with
              <code>action: "reply"</code>. It can also <strong>steer</strong> a
              live child with <code>steer</code>.</span
            >
          </p>
          <div class="sig">
            subagent_supervisor({ action: "reply", message })
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="callout warn">
        <p>
          <span data-lang="pt"
            ><strong>Regra de ouro da escrita:</strong> só
            <em>um</em> trabalhador escreve no mesmo diretório por vez.
            Paralelize leitura, revisão e pesquisa à vontade — mas a escrita é
            em fila. (Para escrita paralela real, use
            <code>worktree: true</code> e isole cada filho numa árvore git
            separada.)</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            ><strong>Golden rule of writing:</strong> only <em>one</em> worker
            writes to the same directory at a time. Parallelize reading, review
            and research freely — but writing is serialized. (For true parallel
            writes, use <code>worktree: true</code> and isolate each child in a
            separate git tree.)</span
          >
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- ============ 4. REAL PI CODE ============ -->
      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">4</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Exemplos reais no Pi</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Real examples in Pi</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="kicker">
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >Quatro trechos — um por padrão — usando a ferramenta
          <code class="inline">subagent()</code> que a extensão
          <code class="inline">pi-subagents</code> registra.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >Four snippets — one per pattern — using the
          <code class="inline">subagent()</code> tool that the
          <code class="inline">pi-subagents</code> extension registers.</span
        >
      </p>

      <h3>
        <span data-lang="pt">① Cadeia — reconhecer, planejar, implementar</span
        ><span data-lang="en">① Chain — scout, plan, implement</span>
      </h3>
      <pre class="block"><span class="g">subagent</span>({
  chain: [
    { <span class="a">agent</span>: <span class="s">"scout"</span>,   <span class="a">task</span>: <span class="s">"Map the auth flow"</span> },
    { <span class="a">agent</span>: <span class="s">"planner"</span>, <span class="a">task</span>: <span class="s">"Plan from {previous}"</span> },
    { <span class="a">agent</span>: <span class="s">"worker"</span>,  <span class="a">task</span>: <span class="s">"Implement the plan from {previous}"</span> }
  ]
});</pre>

      <h3>
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >② Paralelo — três revisores, ângulos diferentes</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >② Parallel — three reviewers, different angles</span
        >
      </h3>
      <pre class="block"><span class="g">subagent</span>({
  tasks: [
    { <span class="a">agent</span>: <span class="s">"reviewer"</span>, <span class="a">task</span>: <span class="s">"Review correctness & regressions"</span> },
    { <span class="a">agent</span>: <span class="s">"reviewer"</span>, <span class="a">task</span>: <span class="s">"Review tests & validation"</span> },
    { <span class="a">agent</span>: <span class="s">"reviewer"</span>, <span class="a">task</span>: <span class="s">"Review simplicity"</span> }
  ],
  concurrency: <span class="k">3</span>,
  context: <span class="s">"fresh"</span>      <span class="c"><span data-lang="pt">// contexto limpo = revisão honesta</span><span data-lang="en">// clean context = honest review</span></span>
});</pre>

      <h3>
        <span data-lang="pt">③ Assíncrono — dispare e continue</span
        ><span data-lang="en">③ Async — fire and continue</span>
      </h3>
      <pre
        class="block"
      ><span class="g">subagent</span>({ <span class="a">agent</span>: <span class="s">"worker"</span>, <span class="a">task</span>: <span class="s">"Run the test suite"</span>, <span class="a">async</span>: <span class="k">true</span> });
<span class="c"><span data-lang="pt">// o gerente segue; Pi avisa (🔔) quando o filho terminar</span><span data-lang="en">// the manager keeps going; Pi notifies (🔔) when the child finishes</span></span></pre>

      <h3>
        <span data-lang="pt">④ Conversa — o filho pergunta, o pai responde</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >④ Conversation — the child asks, the parent replies</span
        >
      </h3>
      <pre
        class="block"
      ><span class="c"><span data-lang="pt">// dentro do trabalhador:</span><span data-lang="en">// inside the worker:</span></span>
<span class="g">contact_supervisor</span>({
  reason: <span class="s">"need_decision"</span>,
  message: <span class="s">"Optimize for readability or performance?"</span>
});

<span class="c"><span data-lang="pt">// dentro do gerente, a resposta chega assim:</span><span data-lang="en">// inside the manager, the reply arrives like this:</span></span>
<span class="g">subagent_supervisor</span>({ action: <span class="s">"reply"</span>, message: <span class="s">"Readability."</span> });</pre>

      <div class="callout key">
        <p>
          <span data-lang="pt"
            ><strong>O caminho Pi-nativo (sem extensão):</strong> o Pi puro
            <em>não</em> tem subagentes por design. A alternativa do autor é
            <strong>tmux</strong> — abra painéis, rode <code>pi</code> em cada
            um, e orquestre à mão (ou encadeie com
            <code>pi --print "..." | pi -p</code>). O
            <code>pi-subagents</code> é a versão estruturada desse mesmo ideia.
            <a
              href="https://mariozechner.at/posts/2025-11-30-pi-coding-agent/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
              >Leia o porquê →</a
            ></span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            ><strong>The native Pi path (no extension):</strong> pure Pi has
            <em>no</em> subagents by design. The author’s alternative is
            <strong>tmux</strong> — open panes, run <code>pi</code> in each, and
            orchestrate by hand (or chain with
            <code>pi --print "..." | pi -p</code>). <code>pi-subagents</code> is
            the structured version of that same idea.
            <a
              href="https://mariozechner.at/posts/2025-11-30-pi-coding-agent/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
              >Read why →</a
            ></span
          >
        </p>
      </div>

