              >The “No sub-agents” section: why pure Pi lacks them and how tmux
              is the manual alternative.</span
            >
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://pi.dev/docs/latest" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            ><strong
              >Pi — <span data-lang="pt">documentação oficial</span
              ><span data-lang="en">official docs</span></strong
            ></a
          >
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt"
              >Modos, sessões e a base sobre a qual a extensão se apoia.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >Modes, sessions and the base the extension builds on.</span
            >
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <div class="callout key">
        <p>
          🗣️
          <strong
            ><span data-lang="pt">Pergunte ao seu professor.</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Ask your teacher.</span></strong
          >
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >Boas perguntas: <em>“como faço dois gerentes se falarem?”</em>,
            <em>“cadeia vs paralelo — e se misturar?”</em>,
            <em>“mostre um loop de revisão real com intercom.”</em></span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >Good questions: <em>“how do two managers talk?”</em>,
            <em>“chain vs parallel — what if I mix?”</em>,
            <em>“show a real review loop with intercom.”</em></span
          >
        </p>
      </div>

      <footer class="lesson-foot">
        <div class="next-card">
          <div class="lbl">
            <span data-lang="pt">Próximo passo →</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Next step →</span>
          </div>
          <div class="t">
            <span data-lang="pt">Monte uma orquestra de verdade</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Build a real orchestra</span>
          </div>
          <p style="margin: 8px 0 0; font-size: 0.85rem">
            <span data-lang="pt"
              >Peça ao Pi:
              <code class="inline"
                >“spawne um reviewer em paralelo pra revisar meu diff”</code
              >
              e observe os trabalhadores aparecerem.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >Ask Pi:
              <code class="inline"
                >“spawn a reviewer in parallel to review my diff”</code
              >
              and watch the workers appear.</span
            >
          </p>
        </div>
        <div style="flex: 0 1 240px">
          <div class="lbl">
            <span data-lang="pt">Revisar</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Review</span>
          </div>
          <p style="margin: 6px 0 0">
            <a href="./0001-the-core-loop.html"
              ><span data-lang="pt">Lição 1 · Core loop</span
              ><span data-lang="en">Lesson 1 · Core loop</span></a
            >
            ·
            <a href="./0006-extensions.html"
              ><span data-lang="pt">Lição 6 · Extensões</span
              ><span data-lang="en">Lesson 6 · Extensions</span></a
            >
            ·
            <a href="./0008-o-mapa-dos-agentes.html"
              ><span data-lang="pt">Lição 8 · O mapa</span
              ><span data-lang="en">Lesson 8 · The map</span></a
            >
          </p>
        </div>
      </footer>
    </article>

    <script>
      /* ===== language engine ===== */
      const TITLE = {
        pt: "Orquestra de agentes — um gerente, muitos trabalhadores",
        en: "Agent orchestra — one manager, many workers",
      };
      const store = {
        get: (k) => {
          try {
            return localStorage.getItem(k);
          } catch {
            return null;
          }
        },
        set: (k, v) => {
          try {
            localStorage.setItem(k, v);
          } catch {}
        },
      };
      let LANG = store.get("pi-lang") || "pt";
      function L(o) {
        return o[LANG];
      }
      const __navSubs = [];
      window.PiI18n = {
        get lang() {
          return LANG;
        },
        on(fn) {
          __navSubs.push(fn);
        },
        L,
      };
      function applyLang(lang) {
        LANG = lang;
        document.body.classList.remove("lang-pt", "lang-en");
        document.body.classList.add("lang-" + lang);
        document.documentElement.lang = lang === "en" ? "en" : "pt-BR";
        document.title = TITLE[lang];
        document.querySelectorAll("svg [data-en]").forEach((t) => {
          t.textContent = lang === "en" ? t.dataset.en : t.dataset.pt;
        });
        document.querySelectorAll(".langswitch button").forEach((b) => {
          b.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(b.dataset.go === lang));
        });
        store.set("pi-lang", lang);
        __navSubs.forEach((f) => {
          try {
            f();
          } catch {}
        });
        matcher.render();
        resetQuizzes();
        sim.reset();
      }
      document.querySelectorAll(".langswitch button").forEach((b) => {
        b.addEventListener("click", () => applyLang(b.dataset.go));
      });

      /* ===== quizzes (data-correct, bilingual feedback) ===== */
      function resetQuizzes() {
        document.querySelectorAll(".quiz").forEach((quiz) => {
          quiz.querySelectorAll(".opt").forEach((o) => {
            o.classList.remove("correct", "wrong");
            o.setAttribute("aria-pressed", "false");
          });
          const v = quiz.querySelector(".verdict");
          v.textContent = "";
          v.className = "verdict";
        });
      }
      (function wireQuizzes() {
        document.querySelectorAll(".quiz").forEach((quiz) => {
          const verdict = quiz.querySelector(".verdict");
          quiz.querySelectorAll(".opt").forEach((button) => {
            button.setAttribute("aria-pressed", "false");
            button.addEventListener("click", () => {
              quiz.querySelectorAll(".opt").forEach((o) => {
                o.classList.remove("correct", "wrong");
                o.setAttribute("aria-pressed", "false");
              });
              const correct = button.dataset.correct === "true";
              button.classList.add(correct ? "correct" : "wrong");
              button.setAttribute("aria-pressed", "true");
              const fb = button.getAttribute(
                LANG === "en" ? "data-fb-en" : "data-fb-pt",
              );
              verdict.textContent = (correct ? "✓ " : "✗ ") + fb;
              verdict.className = "verdict " + (correct ? "ok" : "no");
            });
          });
        });
      })();

      /* ===== GAME 1: pattern matcher (bilingual data) ===== */
      const matcher = (function () {
        const optNames = [
          { key: "Cadeia", pt: "Cadeia", en: "Chain" },
          { key: "Paralelo", pt: "Paralelo", en: "Parallel" },
          { key: "Assíncrono", pt: "Assíncrono", en: "Async" },
          { key: "Conversa", pt: "Conversa", en: "Conversation" },
        ];
        const scenes = [
          {
            t: {
              pt: "Refatorar auth exige mapear o código, depois planejar, depois implementar — cada etapa usa a anterior.",
              en: "Refactoring auth requires mapping the code, then planning, then implementing — each stage uses the previous.",
            },
            a: "Cadeia",
            why: {
              pt: "Cada passo depende do anterior → turnos em sequência (chain).",
              en: "Each step depends on the previous → turns in sequence (chain).",
            },
          },
          {
            t: {
              pt: "Quero três revisões independentes (correção, testes, simplicidade) rodando juntas.",
              en: "I want three independent reviews (correctness, tests, simplicity) running together.",
            },
            a: "Paralelo",
            why: {
              pt: "Passos independentes simultâneos → paralelo (leque).",
              en: "Independent simultaneous steps → parallel (fan-out).",
            },
          },
          {
            t: {
              pt: "Disparei a suite de testes longa; quero continuar code-review enquanto roda.",
              en: "I kicked off the long test suite; I want to keep code-reviewing while it runs.",
            },
            a: "Assíncrono",
            why: {
              pt: "Dispare e continue, seja avisado ao fim → assíncrono (background).",
              en: "Fire and continue, get notified at the end → async (background).",
            },
          },
          {
            t: {
              pt: "O trabalhador encontrou uma escolha de produto e não pode decidir sozinho.",
              en: "The worker hit a product choice and can’t decide alone.",
            },
            a: "Conversa",
            why: {
              pt: "O filho precisa de uma decisão do gerente → intercom (ask/reply).",
              en: "The child needs a decision from the manager → intercom (ask/reply).",
            },
          },
          {
            t: {
              pt: "Preciso ler o banco E pesquisar na web, depois cruzar os dois no gerente.",
              en: "I need to read the database AND research the web, then cross both in the manager.",
            },
            a: "Paralelo",
            why: {
              pt: "Leitura e pesquisa são independentes; rodam juntas e o gerente funde.",
              en: "Reading and research are independent; they run together and the manager merges.",
            },
          },
        ];
        let i = 0,
          score = 0,
          answered = 0;
        const tag = document.getElementById("m-tag");
        const text = document.getElementById("m-text");
        const opts = document.getElementById("m-opts");
        const fb = document.getElementById("m-fb");
        const scoreEl = document.getElementById("m-score");
        const next = document.getElementById("m-next");

        function render() {
          const s = scenes[i];
          tag.textContent =
            (LANG === "en" ? "Scenario " : "Cenário ") +
            (i + 1) +
            " / " +
            scenes.length;
          text.textContent = L(s.t);
          fb.textContent = "";
          fb.className = "fb";
          next.disabled = true;
          opts.replaceChildren();
          optNames.forEach((o) => {
            const b = document.createElement("button");
            b.textContent = L(o);
            b.dataset.name = o.key;
            b.addEventListener("click", () => choose(b, o.key, s));
            opts.appendChild(b);
          });
          scoreEl.textContent =
            (LANG === "en" ? "Correct: " : "Acertos: ") +
            score +
            " / " +
            answered;
        }
        function choose(btn, key, s) {
          [...opts.children].forEach((c) => (c.disabled = true));
          answered++;
          const ok = key === s.a;
          if (ok) score++;
          btn.classList.add(ok ? "right" : "wrong");
          if (!ok) {
            const right = [...opts.children].find(
              (c) => c.dataset.name === s.a,
            );
            if (right) right.classList.add("right");
          }
          fb.textContent = (ok ? "✓ " : "✗ ") + L(s.why);
          fb.className = "fb " + (ok ? "ok" : "");
          scoreEl.textContent =
            (LANG === "en" ? "Correct: " : "Acertos: ") +
            score +
            " / " +
            answered;
          next.disabled = false;
        }
        next.addEventListener("click", () => {
          i = (i + 1) % scenes.length;
          if (i === 0 && answered >= scenes.length) {
            scoreEl.textContent =
              (LANG === "en"
                ? "Round complete! Correct: "
                : "Rodada completa! Acertos: ") +
              score +
              " / " +
              answered +
              (LANG === "en" ? " — restarting." : " — reiniciando.");
          }
          render();
        });
        return { render };
      })();

      /* ===== GAME 2: bus simulator (bilingual log) ===== */
      const sim = (function () {
        const mgr = document.getElementById("n-mgr");
        const wa = document.getElementById("n-wa");
        const wb = document.getElementById("n-wb");
        const wc = document.getElementById("n-wc");
        const packet = document.getElementById("packet");
        const log = document.getElementById("sim-log");
        const controls = document.getElementById("sim-controls");
        let busy = false;
        const POS = {
          mgr: { x: 50, y: 16 },
          wa: { x: 18, y: 78 },
          wb: { x: 50, y: 78 },
          wc: { x: 82, y: 78 },
        };
        const IDLE = {
          pt: "~ barramento ocioso. escolha um padrão acima.",
          en: "~ bus idle. pick a pattern above.",
        };

        function clearNodes() {
          [mgr, wa, wb, wc].forEach((n) =>
            n.classList.remove("active", "ask", "busy"),
          );
        }
        function addRow(text, cls) {
          const row = document.createElement("div");
          row.className = "row " + (cls || "");
          row.textContent = text;
          log.appendChild(row);
          log.scrollTop = log.scrollHeight;
        }
        function reset() {
          log.replaceChildren();
          clearNodes();
          addRow(L(IDLE));
        }
        const wait = (ms) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));
        async function fly(from, to, label, color) {
          packet.textContent = label || "→";
          packet.style.background = color || "var(--violet)";
          packet.style.left = POS[from].x + "%";
          packet.style.top = POS[from].y + "%";
          await wait(40);
          packet.classList.add("show");
          await wait(60);
          packet.style.left = POS[to].x + "%";
          packet.style.top = POS[to].y + "%";
          await wait(560);
          packet.classList.remove("show");
          await wait(220);
        }
        const activate = (node) => node.classList.add("active");

        async function run(mode) {
          if (busy) return;
          busy = true;
          [...controls.children].forEach((b) => (b.disabled = true));
          clearNodes();
          log.replaceChildren();
          mgr.classList.add("active");
          const M = (o) => L(o);

          if (mode === "chain") {
            addRow(
              M({ pt: "gerente inicia cadeia", en: "manager starts chain" }),
              "in",
            );
            await fly("mgr", "wa", "→A", "var(--violet)");
            activate(wa);
            addRow(M({ pt: "A devolve resultado", en: "A returns result" }));
            await fly("wa", "wb", "A→B", "var(--teal)");
            activate(wb);
            addRow(M({ pt: "B devolve resultado", en: "B returns result" }));
            await fly("wb", "wc", "B→C", "var(--teal)");
            activate(wc);
            addRow(M({ pt: "C devolve resultado", en: "C returns result" }));
            await fly("wc", "mgr", "C↑", "var(--teal)");
            addRow(
              M({ pt: "gerente sintetiza ✓", en: "manager synthesizes ✓" }),
              "in",
            );
          } else if (mode === "parallel") {
            addRow(
              M({
                pt: "gerente despacha A, B, C juntos",
                en: "manager dispatches A, B, C together",
              }),
              "in",
            );
            await Promise.all([
              fly("mgr", "wa", "→A", "var(--violet)").then(() => activate(wa)),
              fly("mgr", "wb", "→B", "var(--violet)").then(() => activate(wb)),
              fly("mgr", "wc", "→C", "var(--violet)").then(() => activate(wc)),
            ]);
            addRow(
              M({
                pt: "A, B, C trabalham em paralelo",
                en: "A, B, C work in parallel",
              }),
            );
            await wait(500);
            await Promise.all([
              fly("wa", "mgr", "A↑", "var(--teal)"),
              fly("wb", "mgr", "B↑", "var(--teal)"),
              fly("wc", "mgr", "C↑", "var(--teal)"),
            ]);
            addRow(
              M({
                pt: "gerente funde os resultados ✓",
                en: "manager merges results ✓",
              }),
              "in",
            );
          } else if (mode === "async") {
            addRow(
              M({
                pt: "gerente despacha em background",
                en: "manager dispatches in background",
              }),
              "in",
            );
            mgr.classList.add("busy");
            await Promise.all([
              fly("mgr", "wa", "→A", "var(--violet)").then(() => activate(wa)),
              fly("mgr", "wb", "→B", "var(--violet)").then(() => activate(wb)),
              fly("mgr", "wc", "→C", "var(--violet)").then(() => activate(wc)),
            ]);
            addRow(
              M({
                pt: "gerente faz outra coisa…",
                en: "manager does something else…",
              }),
              "note",
            );
            await wait(900);
            await Promise.all([
              fly("wa", "mgr", "A↑", "var(--teal)"),
              fly("wb", "mgr", "B↑", "var(--teal)"),
              fly("wc", "mgr", "C↑", "var(--teal)"),
            ]);
            mgr.classList.remove("busy");
            addRow(
              M({
                pt: "🔔 notificação: trabalhadores terminaram",
                en: "🔔 notification: workers finished",
              }),
              "note",
            );
            addRow(
              M({
                pt: "gerente retoma e sintetiza ✓",
                en: "manager resumes and synthesizes ✓",
              }),
              "in",
            );
          } else if (mode === "ask") {
            addRow(
              M({ pt: "gerente despacha → B", en: "manager dispatches → B" }),
              "in",
            );
            await fly("mgr", "wb", "→B", "var(--violet)");
            activate(wb);
            await wait(500);
            wb.classList.remove("active");
            wb.classList.add("ask");
            addRow(
              M({
                pt: "B trava: precisa de decisão",
                en: "B halts: needs a decision",
              }),
              "out",
            );
            await fly("wb", "mgr", "?", "var(--amber)");
            addRow(
              M({ pt: "gerente responde", en: "manager replies" }),
              "note",
            );
            await fly("mgr", "wb", "↩", "var(--violet)");
            wb.classList.remove("ask");
            activate(wb);
            await wait(400);
            await fly("wb", "mgr", "B↑", "var(--teal)");
            addRow(
              M({ pt: "B retoma e devolve", en: "B resumes and returns" }),
              "in",
            );
          }

          [...controls.children].forEach((b) => (b.disabled = false));
          busy = false;
        }
        controls.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
          const b = e.target.closest("button[data-run]");
          if (b) run(b.dataset.run);
        });
        return { reset };
      })();

      /* ===== init ===== */
      applyLang(LANG);
    </script>
  </Fragment>
